Antti Sokero's misaligned-source longword copy (xrtg-amix, va2000draw.c,
va2000CopyRun; MIT, Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Antti Sokero, one of the
holders rtgdraw.c's header names), in the RTG layer's copyRun.

copyRun moved two pixels per store only when source and destination
shared their 2-byte phase, and one per store otherwise.  Now it aligns
the destination and, when the source is not longword-aligned, builds each
long from two word reads (the first pixel the high half): every store to
the framebuffer is one aligned long and no access is misaligned.  It
serves the CPU copies within the screen and the direct PutImage, whose
own misaligned long reads of the request go: an odd window x now takes
copyRun's path.

